# class Shadowing { constructor() { this.m = own } m() {} }  seen = new Shadowing().m;  class Plain { m() {} }  other = new Plain().m
# A read goes on to the prototype because nothing is stored under the name on the receiver. Whether the store in the constructor or the read is looked at first depends on the order of the solve,
# so the read takes that step only while nothing is queued, and after the stores that wait: the name that every construction puts on the object hides the method in every order.
# An object that gets no such name inherits the method.
